  "markdown_content": "## Government Directive\\n\\nIndian government officials have instructed banks and traders to avoid using Chinese yuan for settling payments with Russia, according to three government officials and two banking sources familiar with the matter.\\n\\n## Background and Implications\\n\\nThe directive comes amid long-running political differences between India and China, suggesting growing caution in financial dealings between the two Asian powers. The government's move aims to reduce India's financial exposure to Chinese currency while maintaining its trade relationships with Russia.\\n\\nThis development could significantly impact the evolving trade dynamics between India, Russia, and China, particularly in the context of international sanctions and alternative payment mechanisms.",
